249
00:13:54,780 --> 00:13:55,900
Nice try, Kaiba.

250
00:13:59,340 --> 00:14:01,980
Looks like your blue-eyes barrage failed.

251
00:14:02,920 --> 00:14:05,540
That was quite a predictable move, Kaiba,

252
00:14:05,700 --> 00:14:07,877
and one which I was well
prepared to deflect.

253
00:14:07,960 --> 00:14:09,980
So I have emerged untouched.

254
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:11,777
But what about your friend Loomis?

255
00:14:11,860 --> 00:14:12,690
Me?

256
00:14:12,773 --> 00:14:13,603
Yes, Loomis,

257
00:14:13,686 --> 00:14:15,497
don't you wonder what
would have happened had my

258
00:14:15,580 --> 00:14:18,477
blue-eyes white dragon
attacked you instead of Umbra?

259
00:14:18,560 --> 00:14:21,217
Would he have protected
you with his magic card?

260
00:14:21,300 --> 00:14:23,065
Or would he have let you lose?

261
00:14:25,140 --> 00:14:28,357
That's the danger in depending
on someone else to help you

262
00:14:28,440 --> 00:14:31,852
when the reality is there's
only one person you can trust.

263
00:14:32,460 --> 00:14:33,290
Yourself.

264
00:14:33,373 --> 00:14:36,222
And if anyone tells you
otherwise, they're lying.

265
00:14:37,400 --> 00:14:38,230
What?

266
00:14:38,313 --> 00:14:39,580
Don't listen to him!

267
00:14:39,840 --> 00:14:42,737
Of course I would have used
my magic card to help you!

268
00:14:42,820 --> 00:14:46,761
Even though I'm sure you wouldn't
do the same thing for me, Loomis!

269
00:14:47,160 --> 00:14:49,278
Now I get what Kaiba's trying to do!

270
00:14:49,500 --> 00:14:53,397
He noticed that Loomis and Umbra were
beginning to doubt one another's loyalty!

271
00:14:53,480 --> 00:14:57,557
So he's taking advantage of that and
trying to destroy their team trust!

272
00:14:57,640 --> 00:14:58,900
Maybe Kaiba's right!

273
00:14:59,160 --> 00:15:01,177
Umbra seems to be in this for himself!

274
00:15:01,260 --> 00:15:04,997
He probably wants to take all the credit
for winning their Egyptian god cards!

275
00:15:05,080 --> 00:15:07,477
Master Merrick did always like him better.

276
00:15:07,560 --> 00:15:09,997
Well, I'll destroy these
two without his help.

277
00:15:10,080 --> 00:15:11,480
This duel is over!

278
00:15:15,180 --> 00:15:16,120
Check it out.

279
00:15:16,300 --> 00:15:17,397
We're almost there.

280
00:15:17,480 --> 00:15:20,777
I really do appreciate everything
you've done for me, Tristan.

281
00:15:20,860 --> 00:15:23,137
I don't know what I would
have done without your help.

282
00:15:23,220 --> 00:15:28,037
When you updated me on Joey's duels, you
helped give me the courage that I needed.

283
00:15:28,120 --> 00:15:29,577
Don't mention it, Serenity.

284
00:15:29,660 --> 00:15:31,357
I had a great time hanging out with you.

285
00:15:31,440 --> 00:15:35,657
Me too, and thanks for going through all
the trouble to bring me to Battle City.

286
00:15:35,740 --> 00:15:39,217
There's nothing else I'd rather
be doing right now, Serenity.

287
00:15:39,300 --> 00:15:40,130
Wow,

288
00:15:40,213 --> 00:15:43,857
I feel like the luckiest person in the
world to have a friend as awesome as you,

289
00:15:43,940 --> 00:15:44,770
Tristan.

290
00:15:44,853 --> 00:15:45,980
Did she say friend?

291
00:15:46,480 --> 00:15:49,080
Oh, man, I'm stuck in the friend zone!

292
00:15:54,580 --> 00:15:55,840
Joey, it's you!

293
00:15:56,040 --> 00:15:57,397
I'm so glad you're all right.

294
00:15:57,480 --> 00:16:00,217
You've got to help me out of this chair
so we can escape from this rat hole.

295
00:16:00,300 --> 00:16:02,000
Hello? Earth to Joey?

296
00:16:02,260 --> 00:16:04,280
Anybody home in there? Joey?

297
00:16:04,520 --> 00:16:05,380
Are you okay?

298
00:16:05,980 --> 00:16:06,920
Joke's over.

299
00:16:07,720 --> 00:16:08,680
Come on, Joey.

300
00:16:08,860 --> 00:16:10,257
You're freaking me out here.

301
00:16:10,340 --> 00:16:12,560
I am not Joey, you fool.

302
00:16:12,940 --> 00:16:13,940
That's not funny.

303
00:16:15,060 --> 00:16:16,660
What did you do to him?

304
00:16:17,940 --> 00:16:19,160
Now I'll draw.

305
00:16:21,260 --> 00:16:23,540
The magic card, Pot of Greed.

306
00:16:24,380 --> 00:16:28,540
Thanks to this card, I can now draw
two new cards from my deck, Kaiba.

307
00:16:31,380 --> 00:16:33,517
My hand doesn't look very promising,

308
00:16:33,600 --> 00:16:38,217
and with no monsters on the field and
the pending threat of a blue-eyes attack,

309
00:16:38,300 --> 00:16:40,760
I'm in no position to have weak cards.

310
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:48,560
I will place one card face down, and
then I'll activate card exchange!

311
00:16:50,840 --> 00:16:54,057
Laying this card allows
me to exchange my entire

312
00:16:54,140 --> 00:16:57,080
hand with that of any
other duelist on the field.

313
00:16:57,940 --> 00:16:59,480
And I choose you,

314
00:16:59,660 --> 00:17:03,477
Umbra If you're not going
to use your cards to help

315
00:17:03,560 --> 00:17:07,780
me Then I'll simply take
them How dare you All right,

316
00:17:07,920 --> 00:17:13,600
Umbra According to the rules, we swap
hands So give me all of your cards now Here

317
00:17:15,240 --> 00:17:21,017
And now I will activate my face-down
magic card Chosen one If this works,

318
00:17:21,100 --> 00:17:23,180
you two are finished I'll explain

319
00:17:24,020 --> 00:17:27,320
First, I'll place three
cards face down on the field.

320
00:17:27,660 --> 00:17:31,020
And in the center of these
three cards goes the chooser.

321
00:17:33,400 --> 00:17:36,080
The chooser will select
one card at random.

322
00:17:36,380 --> 00:17:40,909
If it chooses one of my two magic cards,
all three cards go to the graveyard.

323
00:17:41,340 --> 00:17:43,340
Those are my cards you're risking.

324
00:17:43,700 --> 00:17:46,582
I'm afraid they're not
your cards anymore, Umbra.

325
00:17:46,960 --> 00:17:49,960
If this doesn't work,
you'll be sorry, Loomis.

326
00:17:50,260 --> 00:17:52,660
Now, chooser, make your selection.

327
00:17:53,180 --> 00:17:57,000
I forgot to mention that if the
chooser selects my third card,

328
00:17:57,240 --> 00:17:59,937
I'll be able to summon an
all-powerful monster to the

329
00:18:00,020 --> 00:18:03,277
field without having to
sacrifice a weaker monster first.

330
00:18:03,360 --> 00:18:05,280
And you'll both be finished.

331
00:18:07,140 --> 00:18:09,460
If this works, I'll be unstoppable.

332
00:18:09,980 --> 00:18:14,274
I'll destroy Kaiba and Yugi on my own,
and Master Merrick will reward me.

333
00:18:14,560 --> 00:18:16,480
It's starting to slow down.

334
00:18:17,300 --> 00:18:18,980
It's choosing a card.

335
00:18:21,080 --> 00:18:21,940
That's it.

336
00:18:24,160 --> 00:18:26,780
It's chosen my ultimate monster!

337
00:18:27,220 --> 00:18:29,080
Now the end is near!

338
00:18:30,640 --> 00:18:34,040
I summon the masked beast, Desgardias!

339
00:18:40,360 --> 00:18:41,760
It's unstoppable!

340
00:18:42,420 --> 00:18:45,560
It's more powerful than
my blue-eyes white dragon!

341
00:18:45,900 --> 00:18:47,420
Very observant, Kaiba!

342
00:18:47,800 --> 00:18:50,557
Desgardias could demolish
your pathetic blue-eyes

343
00:18:50,640 --> 00:18:53,522
white dragon with one
swipe of its almighty claw.

344
00:18:55,260 --> 00:18:58,500
You're lucky the outcome of
your move was successful.

345
00:18:59,640 --> 00:19:04,360
Yes, and now that Desgardias has been
unleashed, there's no stopping it.

346
00:19:04,620 --> 00:19:06,880
My masked creature is so powerful,

347
00:19:07,220 --> 00:19:10,573
you two pitiful duelists won't
stand a chance against it.

348
00:19:10,680 --> 00:19:12,297
And when it's through with you,

349
00:19:12,380 --> 00:19:15,057
your blue eyes will be in
the graveyard and both of

350
00:19:15,140 --> 00:19:18,320
your Egyptian god cards will
belong to Master Merrick.

351
00:19:19,700 --> 00:19:20,700
Oh, no! No!

352
00:19:20,860 --> 00:19:22,677
We've got to defeat their monster!

353
00:19:22,760 --> 00:19:25,057
Otherwise, I may never
see my friends again!

354
00:19:25,140 --> 00:19:28,022
But how can we take down
something that powerful?

355
00:19:28,260 --> 00:19:32,720
And now, the question is, which one
of you fools should I attack first?

356
00:19:33,260 --> 00:19:34,495
Decisions, decisions!

357
00:19:34,840 --> 00:19:36,360
I could attack you, Yugi!

358
00:19:36,640 --> 00:19:39,317
With your useless Magnet
Warriors protecting you,

359
00:19:39,400 --> 00:19:41,871
I'd wipe out the rest of your life points!

360
00:19:42,620 --> 00:19:44,220
Then again, there's Kaiba!

361
00:19:44,560 --> 00:19:48,257
I could attack your blue eyes and rid
the field of that menace for good!

362
00:19:48,340 --> 00:19:51,600
It doesn't really matter
who you attack next,

363
00:19:51,800 --> 00:19:55,657
it's only a matter of time before
both of their life points reach zero,

364
00:19:55,740 --> 00:19:58,857
and they're sent plummeting
into the Shadow Realm forever!

365
00:19:58,940 --> 00:19:59,770
Exactly!

366
00:20:00,020 --> 00:20:04,440
So forget about rescuing your
friends, they belong to Merrick now!
